course: dictionary
lesson: 2234
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Cowboy is one of them: it can mean a rider on a ranch, a hero in a film, a careless worker, or someone who breaks the rules. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «They start taking turns, and on wide bits they walk three abreast like cowboys in a film.» The words «in a film» are the clue. Here cowboys are the heroes of western films who ride horses, not real people working on a ranch.
explain: «Mia's chat has a "weirdo of the week" game, and in week three it's her, for a cowboy hat.» In «cowboy hat», the word cowboy describes the hat. It is a wide hat, the kind cowboys wear in films and stories. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then try it in the sentence.
explain: In British and Australian talk, «cowboy builders» is a warning. It means workers who do careless, bad or dishonest work and often overcharge you. Whenever a word has more than one meaning, swap each meaning into the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Cowboy» can mean a man who rides horses and looks after cattle on a ranch, especially in the western USA.
fact: In films and stories, a cowboy rides horses and wears a wide hat and boots.
fact: In British and Australian informal talk, «cowboy builders» means careless, bad or dishonest workers who often charge too much.
fact: A cowboy can also be a person who acts in a wild, reckless way and ignores the rules.
exercise: «They walk three abreast like cowboys in a film.» What are cowboys in this sentence? | Sailors on big ships | Teachers who take a class on a trip | Farmers who grow wheat | *Characters in western films who ride horses and wear wide hats
exercise: Dad says, «Don't hire cowboy builders, they'll do a bad job and overcharge.» What does cowboy builders mean? | *Careless, dishonest workers who do bad work | Builders who ride horses to work | Very fast builders who finish in one day | Builders who wear wide hats
exercise: In «a cowboy hat», what kind of hat is it? | A hat that makes you invisible | A hat for swimming | A hat made of wool for winter | *A wide hat in the style cowboys wear
test: Jamal says, «He's a cowboy, always breaking the rules and never thinking.» What does cowboy mean here? | *A person who acts wildly and ignores the rules | A person who sells cattle | A film hero who wears boots | A man who rides horses on a ranch
test: Why does a word with more than one meaning need context? | Because all words mean exactly one thing | *Because the sentence shows which meaning fits | Because context only matters in stories | Because dictionaries are always wrong
exam: The advert said, «Cowboy builders, cheap and quick!» What is the warning? | Sign up for a prize at the ranch | They are very kind and helpful, so hire them at once | Cowboys will bring horses to fix your roof | *Be careful: they may do careless, dishonest work
